{
  "id": "remint-preset-set-existing-card",
  "title": "Re-mint: a preset created in the window is kept; assigning it to a card the server had is discarded",
  "covers": [
    "re-mint selection (SYNC.md 10.4 step 1): an op that depends on a window row is re-minted only if the row it writes is a window row",
    "card.preset_set of an existing card to a window preset: unknown_reference, discarded by Re-mint (it writes the shared register preset_id)",
    "card.preset_set of a window card: re-minted with the card"
  ],
  "narrative": [
    "A creates a note and card (seq 1-2) and syncs. Then A's clock jumps 10 days ahead; offline, A creates preset P, assigns P to the existing card, adds a new word (note + card) and assigns P to the new card too.",
    "Meanwhile B flags the existing card (seq 3).",
    "A pushes with the clock still wrong: fsrs_params.created and note.created are clock_ahead; both card.preset_set ops and card.created are unknown_reference (P and the new note do not exist on the server).",
    "The user fixes the clock and runs Re-mint. W = {P, the new note, the new card}. The preset_set of the new card writes a window row (the card is in W): re-minted. The preset_set of the existing card writes the register preset_id of a card every replica has, so its winner would be decided by an estimated time: discarded (SYNC.md 10.4, 'Edits of rows the server already has').",
    "The re-minted creations carry mint_at(t') = their real times (wall(hlc) - 10 days). The existing card keeps the Default preset.",
    "A also reviewed the new card an hour after creating it (unknown_reference). It is re-minted in step 6b with a new id and reviewed_at shifted by the same delta as the creations, so it stays an hour after its card. `remint` lists the inputs; tools/validate.py recomputes the selection and the shift."
  ],
  "devices": {
